            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0954" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6731/195: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-04T17:00:00+02:00">May 4, 1937—5 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. My telegram No. 5, November 6, 4 p.m., from Ankara. I have just received from
                    the Turkish Minister for Foreign Affairs a note proposing the negotiation of an
                    arrangement for reciprocal tariff reductions. I am acknowledging it in
                    accordance with your telegram No. 1, November 19, 6 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
